+## Proposed, awaiting the steward
+
+These are proposals, not decisions. Each was recorded on 2026-10-07 by an agent running `entropy-assessment` on this repo. When the steward decides one, record the decision as a dated, attributed entry below and remove the proposal. Until then the existing instructions stand, and the changes that depend on a proposal are drafted, not applied.
+
+### Proposed: who may change INTENT.md, and who the steward is
+
+**Question**: `INTENT.md` (opening note and closing line), `AGENTS.md` ("Consult INTENT.md for significant decisions") and `skills/local/entropy-guard/SKILL.md` (check 3) each tell a contributor to edit `INTENT.md` when work challenges it. No file names a steward or who decides. Justin Philpott makes the recorded scope decisions in `explorations/2026-03-24-entropy-immune-system-conversation.md` and owns the GitHub repositories this repo links to.
+**Readings**: (a) any contributor, human or agent, may revise `INTENT.md` on their own judgement, noting the date and reason; (b) contributors propose, and `INTENT.md` changes only when the steward decides.
+**Where they diverge**: `INTENT.md`'s lifecycle section does not mention `session-coherence-skill-generator`. Under (a) the next agent edits it; under (b) it records a proposal, as below, and waits.
+**Recommendation**: (b), naming Justin Philpott as steward. `LEARNINGS.md` ("The four-component temporal hierarchy") says intent "should be the most protected and slowest-changing element", and `PHILOSOPHY.md` ranks "intent > machinery > content".
+**Depends on it**: replacing the edit-INTENT instruction in `INTENT.md`, `AGENTS.md` and the local guard (drafted).
+
+### Proposed: which skill writes guards
+
+**Question**: `docs-first-planning-assessment` Phase 2 (Steps 6–8) designs and produces guards; `session-coherence-skill-generator` writes guards to its own requirements at `skills/session-coherence-guard/SKILL.md`. Neither mentions the other, `entropy-assessment` routes only to the first, and `INTENT.md` ("The guard lifecycle") names only the assessment workflow as the generator, while `README.md` and `AGENTS.md` list the second as generating guards. No entry records why `session-coherence-skill-generator` was added.
+**Readings**: (a) each writes guards for its own kind of repo; (b) `session-coherence-skill-generator` is the one guard writer, and `docs-first-planning-assessment` supplies the checks it builds in; (c) `docs-first-planning-assessment` writes guards, and `session-coherence-skill-generator` only bootstraps young repos.
+**Where they diverge**: an external docs-first repo with no guard. Under (a) or (c) Phase 2 produces a combined checklist with no set path; under (b) the generator writes `skills/session-coherence-guard/SKILL.md` with modes, exact commands and safety rules, from Phase 2's checks.
+**Recommendation**: (b). "Consolidate domain generators into single skill" below found that domain knowledge is reference data, not a separate process; the newest entry, "Session-coherence generation should bootstrap young repos", invests in the generator.
+**Depends on it**: `INTENT.md`'s lifecycle section, the `README.md` and `AGENTS.md` rows for the generator, and the handoff in `docs-first-planning-assessment` Phase 2 (drafted).
+
+### Proposed: what the validation batch measures
+
+**Question**: "Farm broader entropic-immunity exploration" below sets the loop as "assess a larger set of open source projects ... and track whether that produces more merged PRs". `INTENT.md` ("Scope boundary and next validation loop"), `README.md` ("Project status") and `TODO.md` set it on docs-first planning repos, tracking clearer session recovery, fewer reintroduced stale ideas and more coherent docs.
+**Readings**: (a) merged PRs on open-source projects; (b) session recovery and coherence on docs-first repos, which may be private.
+**Where they diverge**: a private docs-first planning repo with no pull-request flow counts under (b) and yields nothing under (a).
+**Recommendation**: (b), also recording merged-PR outcomes where a target has a PR flow. `INTENT.md`, `README.md` and `TODO.md` agree on (b), and "Specialize first" narrowed the track to docs-first repos.
+
+### Proposed: when an agent may file an issue on justinphilpott/entropy-guard
+
+**Question**: `skills/entropy-assessment/SKILL.md`, `skills/docs-first-planning-assessment/SKILL.md` and `AGENTS.md` file upstream feedback only when working inside this repo. `skills/guards-integrator/SKILL.md` (Step 7) and "Upstream feedback should be embedded" below also allow it "whenever the local feedback helper is available". The helper runs `gh issue create` against the public repository.
+**Readings**: (a) only when working inside entropy-guard; (b) whenever the helper can be reached, including while assessing another project with entropy-guard checked out.
+**Where they diverge**: `README.md`'s own usage, "Read skills/entropy-assessment/SKILL.md from the entropy-guard repo, then assess [your project path]". At the integrator's last step the agent files a public issue under (b), and not under (a).
+**Recommendation**: (a). Elsewhere, leave the formatted note in the output, as `skills/guards-integrator/SKILL.md` already does when the helper is unavailable. Three of the five places say (a).
+
